<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37875" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prae-rădĭo</span></b> ,
			āre, v. n. and <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>a.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Neutr.</i>, <i>to beam</i> or <i>glitter forth</i> (<b>poet.</b>):
			pilenta praeradiant, Claud. Nupt. Honor. et Mar. 286.—
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Act.</i>, <i>to outshine</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Bacchi conjux Praeradiat stellis signa minora
					suis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. H.
					6, 116</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
